GPU-clear control provenance and dependency notice
-------------------------------------------------
The RMS GPU-clear control is an original MIT-licensed adaptation of the API setup
pattern in switchbrew/switch-examples, commit
669786898205b7beb25ff1731e72982e6d0397d3,
graphics/deko3d/deko_basic/source/main.c. That example repository marks its
examples public domain: https://github.com/switchbrew/switch-examples/blob/669786898205b7beb25ff1731e72982e6d0397d3/README.md
The adaptation omits all shaders, RomFS and external assets. It is not the original
example, and it makes no shader-translation or gameplay claim.

GPU-clear mode links the deko3d library supplied by the SHA-pinned official
devkitPro image (package deko3d 0.5.0-1). Its API/notice reference is
devkitPro/deko3d@5cc144dcf5606fbcd78430f6c62923546e5f9cf4 (v0.5.0).
The image's actual preserved header/archive hashes are recorded by the build;
package version alone is not claimed to prove a source-to-binary correspondence.
The unmodified deko3d Zlib notice follows. The pinned libnx notice is also included
in the build artifact by the existing recipe.

